                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Zhikui Ren",
                        "email": "zhikuiren8@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ZhikuiRen"
                    },
                    "message": "These \"extra\" logs are disabled at compile time and can not be turned on at run time. I think we want to keep the \"debug\". If we want improve, it is better to keep this patch for only porting to the new API and use a separate patch for specific message clean up /improvement."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree that it's ok to only use the patch to convert to use lg2.\n\nBut the 'bool debug' needs to go aswell (in this patch or a follow-up).\n\nOne of the main benefits of lg2 is that it has ```lg2::debug``` which avoids having to do a patch to enable debug logging.\n\nIf 'bool debug' is not removed then you can have situations where lg2::debug is guarded by a ``` if constexpr (debug)``` and then people need to **turn on debug logging AND write a patch**.\n\nWhich is worse than before."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 434,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure, I will improve this in a new patch \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
