            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I think it'd be worth a follow-up patch that removes all the `if constexpr (debug)` conditions:\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-logging/+/76208"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this could be improved in a follow-up patch with respect to:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/anti-patterns.md#ill-defined-data-structuring-in-lg2-message-strings"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 861,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This message looks informational, and is not an error?\n\nI think this should use `lg2::info()`?\n\nMaybe that can be dealt with in the follow-up patch removing `if constexpr (debug)`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 929,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Also should be cleaned up in a follow-up patch wrt https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/anti-patterns.md#ill-defined-data-structuring-in-lg2-message-strings"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 1008,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I just noticed you're quoting integer values in the message string template (`'{NUM}'`). I suggested the quoting for string types because strings can be empty, and that becomes super confusing in the logs. Integers never render as empty strings though. Quoting them doesn't hurt, but it's also not necessary."
                }
            ],
